# Nothing acquired, derived or built is committed. Inputs are declared and fetched;
# outputs are reproducible from them. See the README on reproducibility.
data/raw/
data/interim/
db/
*.ddb
*.pmtiles
*.gpkg
__pycache__/
.venv/
.env
.DS_Store
published/
# Acquired by the viewer, never committed — same rule as data/raw/.
tools/viewer/cache/
# What the map reads: built by `rewt viewer-data` from a finished published/,
# attached to the release, and fetched by pages.yml at deploy time. Building the
# site in a workflow rather than from the branch is what lets this stay uncommitted
# while the whole network is still served.
docs/viewer/data/
vendor/

# The National Library of Scotland tileset catalogue: 2,016 layers, one filled-in
# bucket URL each. Harvested by enumerating a bucket that permits ListBucket, for
# layers whose addresses the Library does not publish itself and asks not to be served
# on a public website. Committing an index it declined to publish is not something to
# do while a letter to maps@nls.uk is unanswered. Local only; see tools/viewer/.gitignore.
tools/nls_layers.json

# Written by pages.yml from a repository secret at deploy time, and never committed.
# The key it holds is origin-restricted to https://docuracy.github.io and is public on
# the deployed site by necessity — a browser cannot request a tile without it. Keeping
# it out of the history is what makes rotation possible: a key in a public repository
# can be rotated but never withdrawn from every clone of that history.
docs/viewer/keys.json
# Runtime state: which session holds which role on THIS machine, now.
.team/

# Harness screenshots from tools/viewer/shot.py --shot. Development output, and they
# sit under docs/ where Jekyll would publish them — a picture of the map that nobody
# curated is exactly the stale artefact this repository spent 3 September on.
docs/viewer/shots/
